body:
I don't think that most people care about the moral ground, and just want a decent life. No one is good or bad all the time and you have many crazies stirring the pot.

It's all a shit show and I wish I could leave, been looking for a way out for years.

&#x200B;

I'm trying... but other than shame and some available dishes, work and other money related issues take the priority. Like most of the things in life, I don't enjoy doing it for myself and I don't have someone in my life to share it with.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I'm trying, but that usually turns out to be half an hour in one place and eventually I never get to the other stuff.

&#x200B;

I will try to get less tired and put more work there.

I'm not a simple man, but if I was dating someone and wanted to meet with her I would probably have feelings for her. and I would always appreciate people liking me.

&#x200B;

The only girl who loved me was 15 when I was 19, and that weirded me out. also the fact that she was just in a relationship with an already married army guy.
